alidate]} {:db/id "q-102797" :question/id #uuid "e225d14b-6814-51a9-af43-900d2917ad01" :question/math-academy-id "q-102797" :question/problem "The function ${y}_{1}(x)={x}^{3}$ is a solution to the equation ${x}^{2}{y}^{″}-6y=0$ for $x>0.$ If ${y}_{2}=u(x){y}_{1}(x)$ is a second solution of the equation, then which of the following equations must be satisfied by $u(x)?$" :question/worked-solution "We're given that\n\n$$\n{y}_{2}(x)=u(x){y}_{1}(x)=u{x}^{3}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating ${y}_{2}=u{x}^{3}$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{2}^{′} & ={u}^{′}{x}^{3}+3u{x}^{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}^{″} & ={u}^{″}{x}^{3}+6{u}^{′}{x}^{2}+6ux.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}({u}^{″}{x}^{3}+6{u}^{′}{x}^{2}+6ux)-6u{x}^{3} & =0 \\\\ {u}^{″}{x}^{5}+6{u}^{′}{x}^{4}+6u{x}^{3}-6u{x}^{3} & =0 \\\\ {u}^{″}{x}^{5}+6{u}^{′}{x}^{4} & =0 \\\\ {x}^{4}({u}^{″}x+6{u}^{′}) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${x}^{4}\\ne 0$ for $x>0,$ we must have\n\n$$\nx{u}^{″}+6{u}^{′}=0.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-102797/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ba3e0748-2a14-547e-b21e-c34251994a94"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-102797"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-102791/selection/5b17a9c111bc851586b9c1af873795d69365adaa586db662837059b61a484964" :answer/id #uuid "f5348148-5daa-58d5-baef-6d4cdf4e84a6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{u}^{″}={e}^{-2x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102791/selection/a0f6a5518a913e02e3a901d1b1181eef033d0ed9402c4e1e964811700bd7187e" :answer/id #uuid "e687c2d7-0fef-5849-989c-b5d7702bcfb0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{u}^{″}=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102791/selection/eeee0536f5d95b7b2c00e0e5b5642866afeb69bb41e25c663eb09bb1410d0839" :answer/id #uuid "aca9bcca-4140-5f61-aeba-5f989e2759f1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{u}^{″}+8u=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102791/selection/796639999d68f449eb29024f16ce32736ca92ceb6f259bdb2a48abbb19800716" :answer/id #uuid "eae148de-88b5-5d9a-a3bf-bbb9b0d4cf6a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{u}^{″}+4u=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102791/selection/305ca33cb8c4f7f7af2646bc88ee2063ccb4e088da068d1876a384a845525473" :answer/id #uuid "2d86807e-183a-5f39-b04a-69f38669aac0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{u}^{″}-4xu=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102791/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f6165270-94dd-57e1-ae78-90b0d82a5ca2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-102791/selection/a0f6a5518a913e02e3a901d1b1181eef033d0ed9402c4e1e964811700bd7187e" :answer-field/choices ["q-102791/selection/5b17a9c111bc851586b9c1af873795d69365adaa586db662837059b61a484964" "q-102791/selection/a0f6a5518a913e02e3a901d1b1181eef033d0ed9402c4e1e964811700bd7187e" "q-102791/selection/eeee0536f5d95b7b2c00e0e5b5642866afeb69bb41e25c663eb09bb1410d0839" "q-102791/selection/796639999d68f449eb29024f16ce32736ca92ceb6f259bdb2a48abbb19800716" "q-102791/selection/305ca33cb8c4f7f7af2646bc88ee2063ccb4e088da068d1876a384a845525473"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-102791" :question/id #uuid "02cdb037-5206-5f07-ac61-66ec161143d6" :question/math-academy-id "q-102791" :question/problem "The function ${y}_{1}(x)={e}^{2x}$ is a solution to the equation ${y}^{″}-4{y}^{′}+4y=0.$ If ${y}_{2}=u(x){y}_{1}(x)$ is a second solution of the equation, then which of the following equations must be satisfied by $u(x)?$" :question/worked-solution "We're given that\n\n$$\n{y}_{2}(x)=u(x){y}_{1}(x)=u{e}^{2x}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating ${y}_{2}=u{e}^{2x}$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{2}^{′} & ={u}^{′}{e}^{2x}+2u{e}^{2x} \\\\ {y}_{2}^{″} & ={u}^{″}{e}^{2x}+4{u}^{′}{e}^{2x}+4u{e}^{2x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({u}^{″}{e}^{2x}+4{u}^{′}{e}^{2x}+4u{e}^{2x})-4({u}^{′}{e}^{2x}+2u{e}^{2x})+4u{e}^{2x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{2x}({u}^{″}+4{u}^{′}+4u-4{u}^{′}-8u+4u) & =0 \\\\ {e}^{2x}{u}^{″} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${e}^{2x}\\ne 0,$  we must have\n\n$$\n{u}^{″}=0.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-102791/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ba3e0748-2a14-547e-b21e-c34251994a94"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-102791"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-64993/selection/0ec9f3d34d3a9d23e2c7df0b4e6345fda1c64e03849e10926179adc06a083b5a" :answer/id #uuid "c1113c41-1136-5bf9-a861-a388bdc07556" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{u}^{″}-16{u}^{′}=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64993/selection/a0f6a5518a913e02e3a901d1b1181eef033d0ed9402c4e1e964811700bd7187e" :answer/id #uuid "31558e27-fbf9-545d-a348-27349d2a7c64" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{u}^{″}=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64993/selection/f8eb2bcd6a6d301442213649e2b25769a10e4b26ebd42b1652a1dfc7982bf162" :answer/id #uuid "d2837b6b-8ef3-51f8-8195-2d8aaf263385" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{u}^{″}-4{u}^{′}=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64993/selection/6743383099ab7bb30ba6ea34326283ea13c3b397dadadc7eceefbe02e399df3c" :answer/id #uuid "cf54638f-8d75-5357-92c8-fc61691dc0c8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{u}^{″}+8{u}^{′}=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64993/selection/b014ad8b2fa1fc38622825a753dfa4ed7d8eb9fae7a4feeaf792946f2d293532" :answer/id #uuid "ee38f740-c9fa-54e1-8d6c-92fc76611289" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{u}^{″}+2{u}^{′}=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64993/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3b50acc6-7f2b-56d7-a93e-b953b5586d1e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-64993/selection/a0f6a5518a913e02e3a901d1b1181eef033d0ed9402c4e1e964811700bd7187e" :answer-field/choices ["q-64993/selection/0ec9f3d34d3a9d23e2c7df0b4e6345fda1c64e03849e10926179adc06a083b5a" "q-64993/selection/a0f6a5518a913e02e3a901d1b1181eef033d0ed9402c4e1e964811700bd7187e" "q-64993/selection/f8eb2bcd6a6d301442213649e2b25769a10e4b26ebd42b1652a1dfc7982bf162" "q-64993/selection/6743383099ab7bb30ba6ea34326283ea13c3b397dadadc7eceefbe02e399df3c" "q-64993/selection/b014ad8b2fa1fc38622825a753dfa4ed7d8eb9fae7a4feeaf792946f2d293532"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-64993" :question/id #uuid "e3f94cd0-0f26-5504-b218-e3f08dc30463" :question/math-academy-id "q-64993" :question/problem "The function ${y}_{1}(x)={e}^{-4x}$ is a solution to the equation ${y}^{″}+8{y}^{′}+16y=0.$ If ${y}_{2}=u(x){y}_{1}(x)$ is a second solution of the equation, then which of the following equations must be satisfied by $u(x)?$" :question/worked-solution "We're given that\n\n$$\n{y}_{2}(x)=u(x){y}_{1}(x)=u{e}^{-4x}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating ${y}_{2}=u{e}^{-4x}$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{2}^{′} & ={u}^{′}{e}^{-4x}-4u{e}^{-4x} \\\\ {y}_{2}^{″} & ={u}^{″}{e}^{-4x}-8{u}^{′}{e}^{-4x}+16u{e}^{-4x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({u}^{″}{e}^{-4x}-8{u}^{′}{e}^{-4x}+16u{e}^{-4x})+8({u}^{′}{e}^{-4x}-4u{e}^{-4x})+16u{e}^{-4x} & =0 \\\\ {u}^{″}{e}^{-4x} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${e}^{-4x}\\ne 0$ for all $x,$ we must have\n\n$$\n{u}^{″}=0.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-64993/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ba3e0748-2a14-547e-b21e-c34251994a94"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-64993"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-90524/selection/292e151885cc565f6d691e96c8a053da4136289ff65a6c8abd6fbbdf2ba0d8fa" :answer/id #uuid "977b18b8-d6a2-5d14-acb7-f85494150aab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{u}^{″}+2{t}^{3}u=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90524/selection/68994b3697fdcdec09db286c70ca6107bf6880306b31e9cda75c5e8988100cce" :answer/id #uuid "8e67f996-1188-5cfa-afe2-c456c6aa8664" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{u}^{″}-{t}^{3}u=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90524/selection/661bcd21335128435d6b2d1c1118bb091f41f83b7d348521581f058f8683ce6d" :answer/id #uuid "1d8e73bb-1fa2-5a2f-9098-5e7e2c6ce8d2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{t}^{3}{u}^{″}-{u}^{′}=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90524/selection/5bf3bf3d96b276f3c7ed79b551eeb8c1f206f586209d0c5222ac8cc41358085a" :answer/id #uuid "ecacf528-0bf9-55d4-826f-1bca91b06409" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t{u}^{″}+3{u}^{′}=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90524/selection/9115b7749bcb8086a9990b9a8df6d9fc81a2e74d262cd6d35fbf37566a2f6af0" :answer/id #uuid "365b9b3b-99ff-5d37-bce5-5c8b652ae1b7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{u}^{″}+t{u}^{′}=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90524/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "40fbb617-db41-5064-bb4f-1877a2022e9e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-90524/selection/5bf3bf3d96b276f3c7ed79b551eeb8c1f206f586209d0c5222ac8cc41358085a" :answer-field/choices ["q-90524/selection/292e151885cc565f6d691e96c8a053da4136289ff65a6c8abd6fbbdf2ba0d8fa" "q-90524/selection/68994b3697fdcdec09db286c70ca6107bf6880306b31e9cda75c5e8988100cce" "q-90524/selection/661bcd21335128435d6b2d1c1118bb091f41f83b7d348521581f058f8683ce6d" "q-90524/selection/5bf3bf3d96b276f3c7ed79b551eeb8c1f206f586209d0c5222ac8cc41358085a" "q-90524/selection/9115b7749bcb8086a9990b9a8df6d9fc81a2e74d262cd6d35fbf37566a2f6af0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-90524" :question/id #uuid "a9ab006c-953f-5a4b-abd9-63aa572d2d25" :question/math-academy-id "q-90524" :question/problem "The function ${y}_{1}(t)={t}^{3}$ is a solution to the equation ${t}^{2}{y}^{″}-3t{y}^{′}+3y=0$ for $t>0.$ If ${y}_{2}=u(t){y}_{1}(t)$ is a second solution of the equation, then which of the following equations must be satisfied by $u(t)?$" :question/worked-solution "We're given that\n\n$$\n{y}_{2}(t)=u(t){y}_{1}(t)=u{t}^{3}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating ${y}_{2}=u{t}^{3}$ with respect to $t$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{2}^{′} & ={u}^{′}{t}^{3}+3u{t}^{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}^{″} & ={u}^{″}{t}^{3}+6{u}^{′}{t}^{2}+6ut.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2}({u}^{″}{t}^{3}+6{u}^{′}{t}^{2}+6ut)-3t({u}^{′}{t}^{3}+3u{t}^{2})+3u{t}^{3} & =0 \\\\ {t}^{3}({u}^{″}{t}^{2}+6{u}^{′}t+6u-3{u}^{′}t-9u+3u) & =0 \\\\ {t}^{3}({u}^{″}{t}^{2}+3{u}^{′}t) & =0 \\\\ {t}^{4}({u}^{″}t+3{u}^{′}) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${t}^{4}\\ne 0$ for $t>0,$ we must have\n\n$$\nt{u}^{″}+3{u}^{′}=0.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-90524/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ba3e0748-2a14-547e-b21e-c34251994a94"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-90524"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-64989/selection/03aaedb91e15b1b9a35d29fb4b693d157e287cdd0731b4a8c384ce5d1bc197e2" :answer/id #uuid "44c6b3e9-b294-59c7-ba56-175d7c1bd6db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{u}^{″}-{u}^{′}=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64989/selection/3a333b73a577092e31068e3138092b0fd7127b894ce6cea29af4f1086d5985d8" :answer/id #uuid "168b8500-96b4-502b-9131-120eb713112c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{u}^{″}+5{u}^{′}=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64989/selection/61cb59a9113c81ced5db9abfe0e999d0ff8018dc38da6a4e5d6b1b0fca62ab41" :answer/id #uuid "a31c0423-1518-5b70-bfe4-964bfc0d580c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{u}^{″}+{u}^{′}=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64989/selection/e68853243e0e082a69870fab394e164bdc318f714f20383b